      "captions": {
        "__figure__": "Neuronal populations flexibly encode diverse stimuli. An original demonstration composed from public Allen Institute data; anatomy and recordings come from separate specimens, and the graph links are response similarities, not synapses.",
        "text_mu1xnvk7o6pj_1": "Visual cortical areas on the Allen CCFv3 brain surface in an oblique dorsal view (inset, lateral view); VISl is the recorded area.",
        "text_mu1xnw0etczw_1": "Reconstructed neurons from the Allen Cell Types Database at one scale, pia upward.",
        "text_mu1xnwgwydva_1": "Trial-averaged, per-cell standardized responses of all 143 cells to eight drift directions at 2 Hz, grouped by preferred direction and ordered by response latency.",
        "text_mu1xnwxjiyw3_1": "Four example cells: trial-averaged ΔF/F for every direction (shaded, 2 s grating; one vertical scale per row) and their polar tuning, with the preferred direction marked.",
        "text_mu1xnxdpmqo8_1": "Population trajectories in one three-dimensional PCA basis; saturated segments are stimulus frames, circles onset and squares offset.",
        "text_mu1xnxuka6c3_1": "Signal-correlation matrix ordered by preferred direction.",
        "text_mu1xnyaz2zxv_1": "Cells arranged by preferred direction with links for pairs whose signal correlation is at least 0.6.",
        "text_mu1xnyrc9efz_1": "PCA of the standardized condition means; contours enclose 40, 70 and 90% of the density.",
        "text_mu1xnz86sdhf_1": "Circular orientation versus direction selectivity with marginal distributions.",
        "text_mu1xnzp3qkzx_1": "Temporal-frequency tuning at each cell's preferred direction (mean ± s.e.m.; bands, 10–90% and interquartile ranges; bars, share of cells preferring each frequency).",
        "text_mu1xo062t6cc_1": "Number of cells preferring each direction. Colours throughout follow the drift-direction key."
      }
    },
